---
// src/pages/index.astro
import '../styles/global.css';
import Topbar from "../components/Topbar.astro";
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
      <meta charset="UTF-8" />
      <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
      <title>25CollectiveCo</title>
      <meta name="description" content="25CollectiveCo - Born to be Human." />
      <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    </Fragment>

    <Topbar />

    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <header class="hero">
      <h1>Born to be Human.</h1>
      <h3>Technology should make us more human, not less.</h3>
      <p class="motto">A collective building focused products and communities <br>
      to stay present in a permanently connected world.</p>
      <p class="motto">↓</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content Sections -->
    <main>
      <!-- Current Projects Section -->
      <section id="projects" class="section">
        <h2>Projects</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <h4><b>BMP</b> | 02/26</h4>
          <h5>Live</h5>
          <p class="motto">A running plan builder grounded in peer-reviewed sports science and real training data. Pick a proven
          coaching method (Daniels, Pfitzinger, Hansons, 80/20, Higdon) and it is applied to your actual activity history, delivering
          a complete plan you own as spreadsheet, PDF and calendar files. Instead of subscriptions, AI-generated guesswork, or
          one-size-fits-all templates: one payment, no account, no stored data. Your activity file is processed in your browser
          and never leaves it. (<a href="https://bmprun.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bmprun.com</a>)</p>
          <h4><b>RIKENNECT</b> | 01/26</h4>
          <h5>Live</h5>
          <p class="motto">A faceless media umbrella using reality and statistical context to counter
          social media illusion, share common knowledge, and reduce the pressure embedded in digital
          narratives pushed by algorithms. Now publishing 21 reels a week per brand, end to end on autopilot.
          (Tools: Claude Sonnet 4.5, Kokoro TTS, OpenAI Whisper, Stable Diffusion 1.5,
          OpenCV, FFmpeg, Pillow, PyTorch (MPS), Google Sheets API, Discord Bot)</p>
          <h4><b>25CC</b> | 01/26</h4>
          <h5>Live</h5>
          <p class="motto">Portfolio of early-stage projects in emerging and applied technologies. These
          projects explore how to leverage modern technical capabilities while maintaining a strong focus
          on real-world utility, intentional design, and reduced reliance on constant screen interaction.
          The work is ongoing and iterative, with an emphasis on experimentation, validation, and shipping,
          and is written up every week on the <a href="/blog">blog</a>.</p>
          <h4><b>JARVIS</b> | 09/26</h4>
          <h5>Live</h5>
          <p class="motto">An open-source operating system for running many projects alongside AI agents. One dashboard holds
          every checklist, plan and decision; a local agent picks up the work, builds it on a branch and opens a pull request,
          and nothing merges without a human. Every Monday, advisor reviews read what actually happened that week and say what
          to change. Built to keep the human the decision-maker, not the bottleneck.</p>
          <h4><b>WADEE</b> | 03/26</h4>
          <h5>Beta</h5>
          <p class="motto">Your news briefing as a phone call you can talk back to, plus SMS and email. No app, no feed, no
          infinite scroll. Hundreds of sources are clustered into the few stories that matter for your topics, and a host walks
          you through them: skip, go deeper, or hear the other side, by voice or keypad. Knowledge compounds instead of
          competing with your day. Bilingual English and French from day one.</p>
          <h4><b>KAKEE</b> | 09/26</h4>
          <h5>In Development</h5>
          <p class="motto">Fraud protection for seniors, Quebec first, in French and English. Forward a text or an email,
          photograph a letter or describe a call, and get one clear answer: real (with the verified number to call back), scam,
          or unsure. A verified directory of official contacts and a family circle the senior controls restore clarity,
          confirmation, and human control in digital interactions that are too often irreversible. AI supports the judgement,
          it never replaces it.</p>
          <h4><b>BDLX-P</b> | 02/26</h4>
          <h5>In Development</h5>
          <p class="motto">An image story generator built around one hard problem: consistency. The same character, recognisable
          from the first frame to the last, across a large cast and shifting art styles, with lettering kept as real text instead
          of generated pixels. The current build is a private first edition; the end goal is a one-page product generator,
          one story in, one finished page out.</p>
          <h4><b>HUMANSIGNAL</b> | 26</h4>
          <h5>Backlog</h5>
          <p class="motto">A system for understanding when professional relationships actually matter. Instead 
          of encouraging constant outreach or performance-driven networking, it helps you recognize moments of 
          relevance, shared context, and natural alignment. So connection happens with intent, timing, and 
          respect, rather than pressure or habit.</p>
          <h4><b>KAYZN</b> | 23</h4>
          <h5>Backlog</h5>
          <p class="motto">Kayzn operates where research, culture, and scale intersect. Participation is driven 
          through contemporary channels, while AI is applied at the analysis stage to translate engagement at 
          scale into consumer insight grounded in real-world behavior.</p>
          <h4><b>LIFEKEY</b> | 21</h4>
          <h5>Backlog</h5>
          <p class="motto">A blockchain-backed health data layer focused on continuity, ownership, and trust. It allows personal medical 
          information to be securely managed and shared without relying on disconnected institutional databases.</p>       
          
          <!-- Add your projects here -->
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- About Section -->
      <section id="about" class="section">
        <h2>About</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <p class="motto">25 Collective Co is an independent body of work centered on building and testing early-stage projects in emerging 
          and applied technologies. The focus is on real-world utility, intentional design, and systems that reduce unnecessary 
          friction, abstraction, and dependence on constant screen interaction. The work is ongoing and iterative, shaped by 
          experimentation, validation, and shipping rather than fixed outcomes.
          <br><br>This approach is informed by years of experience working across diverse teams and global environments, including 
          periods of growth, transformation, and operational strain. Having worked closely with roles ranging from entry-level 
          contributors to executive leadership, the emphasis has consistently been on listening, adapting, and building tools 
          and processes that support sustainable execution. 25 Collective Co represents a continuation of that trajectory: a space 
          to explore how modern technical capabilities can be applied thoughtfully, with resilience, clarity, and long-term 
          value in mind.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact Section -->
      <section id="contact" class="section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <p class="motto">Get in touch with us:</p>
          <p class="motto">Email: <a href="mailto:hello25cc@gmail.com">Hello25CC</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
      <div class="footer-content">
        <p class="motto">© 2026 25CollectiveCo</p>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <!-- Progressive enhancement for tab visibility toggling -->
    <script>
      // Simple tab behavior enhancement (works without JS too via anchors)
      const tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-link');
      const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section');
      
      tabs.forEach(tab => {
        tab.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
          const href = tab.getAttribute('href');
          if (href && href.startsWith('#')) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const targetSection = document.querySelector(href);
            if (targetSection) {
              targetSection.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
            }
          }
        });
      });
    </script>
</BaseLayout>